sweet: tell surya when iOS turns the display off and on

RequestPowerChange calls surya_display_power() (bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c, 0900):
double tap to wake, the torch's long press and the notification LED depend on it.

Also (22.10) counters for suryastat=1 (bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c reads them):
swaps, swaps whose first layer samples like the previous one, panel copies
and their time, vsync ticks, and the panel memory for the copy speed test.
suryafb=1 (22.10, wishes/04 step 6): the panel copy runs on its own kernel
thread instead of inside the vsync timer, the timer keeps absolute deadlines
(wakeAtTime) so copies no longer stretch its period, and SwapWait waits (at
most 50 ms) until the pending frame has been copied, so CoreAnimation gets
real back-pressure instead of rendering frames nobody shows. Without the
boot-arg the old path is unchanged.
suryafb2x=1 (22.10, wishes/04 step 8): the display is presented as 750x1624
(the same 375x812 points at @2x: 2.25x fewer pixels for the CPU rasterizer)
and the copy thread scales each layer up to the panel, nearest neighbour.
Needs suryafb=1, /chosen/display-scale 2 in the ADT (scripts/adt-scale.py)
and the MobileGestalt cache truncated once (surya_fb2x_reset_cache, 0900).
The @2x scaling copy (22.10, 8-9 ms a frame at first): clamped column range,
unrolled row loop, rows with the same source copied from the row above.
